From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
Subject: [PATCH net] ionic: free every temporary queue after a queue count
 change

ionic_reconfigure_queues() allocates the new rings in temporary qcqs,
swaps their contents with the live ones, and frees the temporaries,
which then hold the old rings. The loop that frees them runs up to
qparam->nxqs, but by then lif->nxqs and qparam->nxqs have been swapped,
so it runs up to the old queue count.

When the count grows into an index that has no qcq yet, a short
placeholder qcq is allocated for the swap, and its rings and page pool
end up in the temporary of that index, which is beyond the old count
and is never freed. The qcq structs are devm allocations and go away at
unbind, but the DMA allocations do not, and the page pool stays listed
with a pointer to the freed NAPI:

  ip link set $IF down; ethtool -L $IF combined 2; ip link set $IF up
  ethtool -L $IF combined 4; rmmod ionic

  DMA-API: pci 0000:01:00.0: device driver has pending DMA allocations
  while released from device [count=12]

and a later page pool dump over netlink reads the freed NAPI:

  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in page_pool_nl_fill+0x690/0x730

Free the temporaries up to the larger of the two counts. The arrays
have room for every queue, and the loop already skips the entries that
were never allocated.
---
Not part of the Rx header split series; found while testing it, and
reproduced with the unmodified v7.4-rc3 driver. No Fixes: tag yet (the
commit that introduced the swap was not looked up). Tested in a guest
on an emulated ionic: the sequence above no longer leaves pending DMA
allocations or a listed page pool.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c
index 22d1e4b6d61b..3ef3344faba0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c
@@ -3147,8 +3147,11 @@ err_out_reinit_unlock:
 		err = ionic_start_queues_reconfig(lif);
 
 err_out:
-	/* free old allocs without cleaning intr */
-	for (i = 0; i < qparam->nxqs; i++) {
+	/* free old allocs without cleaning intr; the counts may have been
+	 * swapped above, and a placeholder's rings end up in the temporary
+	 * qcq of an index beyond the old count
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < max(qparam->nxqs, lif->nxqs); i++) {
 		if (tx_qcqs && tx_qcqs[i]) {
 			tx_qcqs[i]->flags &= ~IONIC_QCQ_F_INTR;
 			ionic_qcq_free(lif, tx_qcqs[i]);
-- 
